TARGET SYSTEM SPECIFICATION: VocalRefine AI
1. Project Overview & Architecture
Build a full-stack web application called "VocalRefine AI" that empowers speakers to analyze their communication flaws (specifically filler words, pacing, and hesitancy) and hear a re-synthesized, flawless version of their speech generated in their own cloned voice.
Tech Stack Specifications:
Frontend: React (Vite, TypeScript), Tailwind CSS, Lucide React icons.
Backend: Node.js, Express, TypeScript.
APIs:
Fish Audio API: Custom Voice Model Training (/v1/model) and High-Fidelity Text-to-Speech (/v1/tts).
Google Gemini API (gemini-1.5-pro): Multimodal Audio Analysis, Filler Extraction, and Jordan Peterson-style Communication Coaching & Screenplay Refinement.
Audio Processing: Backend fluent-ffmpeg for normalizing audio buffers, converting format encodings, and preparing training audio slices.
2. End-to-End User & System Workflow
Step 1: Voice Calibration & Model Training (Post-Processing Setup)
User records a 30-60 second baseline reading or uploads a clean voice sample.
Backend receives the audio file, uses fluent-ffmpeg to convert it to standard .wav (16kHz, mono), and uploads it to Fish Audio API to train/create a custom Voice Model ID.
Save the returned model_id in session storage or state for downstream TTS synthesis.
Step 2: Speech Recording & Communication Audit
User records their raw spoken thought, narrative, or speech (with natural fillers like "um", "like", "you know", "basically").
Backend passes the raw audio to Google Gemini 1.5 Pro.
Gemini performs audio-level and lexical analysis, returning a strict JSON response containing:
Filler Density Index (%) and exact filler frequency counts.
Raw Transcript vs. Refined "Flawless" Script (with zero fillers, polished transitions, and [pause] indicators).
"Peterson Audit": Unapologetic, constructive feedback analyzing where the speaker lacks conviction or hides behind verbal crutches.
Screenplay/Dialogue Adaptation: Formatted screenplay script extending their idea into a structured conversation.
Step 3: Fresh Voice Re-Synthesis
Frontend displays analysis metrics and the Refined Script.
User clicks "Re-Synthesize in My Refined Voice".
Backend takes the clean, polished script and calls Fish Audio TTS API using the user's cloned model_id created in Step 1.
An entirely fresh, clear audio track is generated and returned to the client for playback side-by-side with the original recording.
